WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.453
The security solution says it took action.

2
00:00:03.453 --> 00:00:04.325
Did it work?

3
00:00:04.325 --> 00:00:12.975
In this demonstration I check three actions from the school: first the event the antivirus wrote, then the host itself.

4
00:00:14.076 --> 00:00:18.867
The action events, from the Defender Operational logs.

5
00:00:18.867 --> 00:00:21.529
Event 1117 means action taken.

6
00:00:21.529 --> 00:00:28.716
Event 1118 means the action failed: here, the file was in use by another process.

7
00:00:29.815 --> 00:00:36.537
Now the after-action check: someone looked on each computer for the file.

8
00:00:36.537 --> 00:00:39.300
On LIB-PC-02 the file is gone.

9
00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:46.666
On MKT-PC-04 the file is still present, even though event 1117 said quarantined.

10
00:00:46.666 --> 00:00:52.927
And on REG-PC-01 it is present, as you would expect after a failure.

11
00:00:54.027 --> 00:00:56.706
So only one action is verified.

12
00:00:56.706 --> 00:01:06.469
MKT-PC-04 is the dangerous one: the console looks fine, but the infected installer is still on the shared folder.

13
00:01:06.469 --> 00:01:12.085
An action you did not verify is an action you only hope happened.

14
00:01:12.085 --> 00:01:19.516
Both MKT-PC-04 and REG-PC-01 are escalated to Tier 2, which we will practise tomorrow.

15
00:01:20.615 --> 00:01:21.503
Your turn.

16
00:01:21.503 --> 00:01:26.298
In the CTM Virtual Lab, choose Day 8 and Activity 8.2.

17
00:01:26.298 --> 00:01:29.494
Six actions on the bank's computers.

18
00:01:29.494 --> 00:01:38.640
For each one, read the event and the after-action check, and decide: verified, not verified, or failed.

